# Call-Scope Authorization

Internal voice/CRM/scheduling/knowledge/handoff APIs must not rely on a shared service token alone in production.

## Production

- `REQUIRE_CALL_SCOPE=true` (enforced by `require_production_settings`)
- Installer and compose must write/pin this — never omit it from production env generation
- Expiry rule: reject when `exp <= now` (RFC 7519)

## Verify matrix (fail closed)

| Case | Result |
|------|--------|
| Missing scope | 401 |
| Tampered / bad sig | 401 |
| Expired | 401 |
| Wrong tenant | 403 |
| Wrong call | 403 |
| Valid scope | 200 |

Body/query/headers must not override tenant or call identity from the verified scope.

## Voice agent

Send `X-Call-Scope` on platform tool calls. Do not invent tenant IDs in tool payloads.

See: `docs/CALL_AUTHORIZATION.md`
